      "id": "akw872g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Factors Affecting Climate of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "India's climate is broadly categorized as a Tropical Monsoon type, shaped by its physiography and latitude.",
        "The South-West Monsoon is divided into two primary branches: the Arabian Sea Branch and the Bay of Bengal Branch.",
        "Local winds play a crucial role in regional weather transitions, including Loo, Kalbaisakhi (Nor'westers), and Mango Showers.",
        "Global atmospheric-oceanic phenomena such as El Niño and La Niña exert a significant influence on the strength and rainfall yield of the Indian Monsoon."
      ],
      "id": "ztxofft"
    },
