      "content": "7. El Niño and La Niña Effect"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Frequently tested: Pre-monsoon local winds and their regional names (e.g., Kalbaisakhi in West Bengal, Mango Showers in Kerala/Karnataka, Loo in Northern Plains).",
        "Crucial distinction: El Niño correlates with deficient monsoon rainfall/droughts in India, whereas La Niña brings strong, abundant rainfall.",
        "Identify the path and distribution features of the Arabian Sea Branch vs. the Bay of Bengal Branch during the South-West Monsoon season."
      ],
